        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "docs(slack): clarify group DM bot membership",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a docs gap where Slack users can read the `dm.groupEnabled` and\n`dm.groupChannels` settings and reasonably assume those settings can make\nOpenClaw see an existing group DM after someone mentions the bot.\n\nSlack group DMs (MPDMs) do not work that way: if the app is not already a\nmember of the MPDM, Slack does not deliver the conversation to the app.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds a Slack docs subsection explaining that `@YourBot` in an existing\ngroup DM does not add the app or make the MPDM visible to it. It also clarifies\nthat `dm.groupEnabled` and `dm.groupChannels` only filter MPDMs Slack already\ndelivers, and it links that explanation from the channel config reference.\n\nThe documented workarounds are the Slack-supported paths: convert the group DM\nto a private channel and invite the app, or have the app open a new MPDM with\n`conversations.open`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators get a clearer answer when Slack group-DM routing appears broken: no\nOpenClaw config can grant visibility into an MPDM the app never joined. The docs\nnow point users to the two working setup paths instead of leaving them to chase\n`dm.groupEnabled` / `dm.groupChannels` as a fix.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- AI-assisted docs PR prepared by Codex, with a Claude Foreman Opus review pass\n  before push.\n- Docs-only change.\n- Ran `pnpm docs:list` before editing docs.\n- Ran `pnpm check:docs`:\n  - `format:docs:check`\n  - `lint:docs`\n  - `docs:check-mdx`\n  - `docs:check-i18n-glossary`\n  - `docs:check-links`\n  - `docs:map:check`\n- Regenerated `docs/docs_map.md` with `pnpm docs:map:gen`.\n- Ran `git diff --check`.\n- Verified the public diff contains no private Slack channel IDs, local project\n  paths, or security-advisory details.\n- Reviewed by Claude Foreman on Opus before push. Foreman flagged the original\n  workaround wording as too broad, so the final text now uses the narrower\n  documented bot-token `conversations.open` path.\n",
